# No line-ending conversion, in either direction, for anything.
#
# This repo is a byte mirror: claude/, codex/, agents/ and memory/ hold exactly what
# sync.ps1 -Mode push read off the live machine (some files CRLF, some LF, a couple mixed -
# all of it the truth being carried), and a restore is only correct if a fresh clone
# materializes those same bytes. Under core.autocrlf=true - this machine's global setting -
# an unpinned checkout rewrote every LF text file to CRLF, so a new machine restored
# byte-different files while every git operation printed line-ending warnings.
#
# One total rule rather than per-tree rules on purpose: a new mirrored tree added to the
# manifest is then pinned by default instead of silently converted until someone notices.
# Repo-native files (*.ps1, *.md, tooling) are authored on Windows and their working-copy
# bytes are canonical too; the eol-sensitive ones, the `.sh` hooks under .claude/hooks/, are
# already LF on disk and -text keeps them that way.
* -text

# Issue 87: these three project files under .claude/ are read (and, on Windows,
# text-mode re-serialized) by Claude Code and any admin tool that touches them
# at session start. Every Windows text-mode writer (Notepad, VS Code default
# save on Windows, PowerShell 5.1 `Get-Content` + `Set-Content`, an installer's
# rewrite) produces CRLF byte-for-byte. Under `* -text` above, git does NO EOL
# conversion; if the blob is LF and the working-copy write is CRLF, `git status`
# reports a phantom ` M` on every fresh worktree while `git diff -w
# --ignore-cr-at-eol` prints nothing (reproduced 2026-09-03 on two worktrees at
# once, and 2026-09-14 on a fresh clone).
#
# The fix is byte-stability, not writer identification: store the blob as CRLF
# so a Windows text-mode writer's output matches the blob byte-for-byte. The
# explicit `-text` below is redundant with `* -text` and stops a later rule
# that removes `-text` (e.g. `.claude/** text`) from re-enabling autocrlf on
# these three files and re-opening the phantom.
.claude/session.json -text
.claude/settings.json -text
.claude/workflows/ticket-fleet.js -text
